    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Brophy Estates are delighted to bring number 12 St. Sylvester Villas, Malahide, to the market. Occupying a wonderful position within one of Malahide’s most established residential enclaves, No. 12 St. Sylvester Villas is an appealing cottage-style home combining traditional character with an exceptional village location. Malahide Castle and Demesne is quite literally on the doorstep, while a leisurely stroll brings you to the heart of Malahide Village, with its renowned selection of restaurants, cafés, boutiques and local amenities. Excellent schools and transport links, including Malahide DART Station, are also within easy reach, adding to the considerable appeal of this superbly located home.\r\nTucked away within a quiet cul-de-sac, No. 12 enjoys a wonderful sense of privacy and tranquillity. One of the property's most impressive features is its beautiful, long south-facing rear garden. Mature and exceptionally private, this 25mtr long garden enjoys excellent natural light throughout the day and provides a wonderful setting for outdoor dining, entertaining, and family life. Its generous proportions also offer considerable potential for a purchaser wishing to further enhance the property, subject to any necessary planning permission.\r\nThe traditional cottage-style façade creates an inviting first impression, while internally the property offers deceptively spacious and versatile accommodation. The layout includes a welcoming entrance hall, comfortable living accommodation, kitchen, three bedrooms, and two bathrooms, a particularly valuable feature for a home of this style.\r\nAdding to the property’s appeal is a versatile attic room, offering valuable additional space and flexibility together with the second bathroom.  This area could lend itself to a variety of uses depending on the purchaser's requirements, such as a home office, study, hobby room or additional storage. The current owners use it as an additional bedroom. \r\nThe combination of the property's traditional character, surprisingly generous accommodation, and exceptionally long south-facing garden makes No. 12 a particularly appealing home. It should attract interest from a broad range of purchasers, whether downsizers seeking a home close to Malahide Village, first-time buyers, or families looking to establish themselves in this highly desirable location.\r\nMalahide itself is one of North County Dublin's most sought-after coastal villages, renowned for its vibrant atmosphere, excellent restaurants, cafés, boutiques and extensive recreational amenities. Malahide Castle and Demesne is virtually on the doorstep, offering acres of parkland and woodland walks, while the Marina, beach and picturesque coastline are also within easy reach.\r\nExcellent transport connections include the DART and regular bus services, providing convenient access to Dublin City Centre and surrounding areas. A wide range of sporting facilities are available locally, including GAA, rugby, tennis, cricket, hockey, sailing and golf.\r\nNo. 12 St. Sylvester Villas represents a rare opportunity to acquire a character-filled home in an exceptional Malahide location, combining a peaceful cul-de-sac setting with three bedrooms, two bathrooms, an attic room, and a magnificent long south-facing rear garden — all within walking distance of Malahide Village and Castle."
      },
